---
description: Ask the user to confirm whenever a request is genuinely unclear or uncertain
alwaysApply: true
---

# Confirm Genuine Uncertainty

- If a request has more than one materially different interpretation, ask the user which one they intend before changing code or external systems.
- If required information cannot be established safely from the repository or other available evidence, ask rather than guessing.
- Do not ask redundant questions when the user has already supplied the answer or the answer can be verified read-only.
- Continue independent, clearly in-scope work while waiting whenever possible.

